<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
<content>
<section id="fs-id1165135194497">
<title>Technology</title>
<exercise id="fs-id1165137780865"><problem id="fs-id1165137780867">
<para id="fs-id1165135641711">Graph <m:math>
<m:mrow>
<m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac>
<m:mn>1</m:mn>
<m:mrow>
<m:msup>
<m:mi>x</m:mi>
<m:mn>2</m:mn>
</m:msup>
</m:mrow>
</m:mfrac>
</m:mrow>
</m:math> on the viewing window <m:math>
<m:mrow>
<m:mo stretchy="false">[</m:mo><m:mn>−0.5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>−0.1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">]</m:mo></m:mrow>
</m:math> and <m:math>
<m:mrow>
<m:mo stretchy="false">[</m:mo><m:mn>0.1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">]</m:mo><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow>
</m:math> Determine the corresponding range for the viewing window. Show the graphs.</para></problem>
<solution id="fs-id1165137501974">

<media id="fs-id1165134258632" alt="Graph of the equation from [-0.5, -0.1].">
<image mime-type="image/jpg" src="../../media/CNX_Precalc_Figure_01_02_221.jpg"/>
</media>

<para id="fs-id1165135191028">window: <m:math>
<m:mrow>
<m:mo stretchy="false">[</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">]</m:mo><m:mo>;</m:mo></m:mrow>
</m:math> range: <m:math>
<m:mrow>
<m:mo stretchy="false">[</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.5em"/><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">]</m:mo></m:mrow>
</m:math>
</para>

<media id="fs-id1165137442910" alt="Graph of the equation from [0.1, 0.5].">
<image mime-type="image/jpg" src="../../media/CNX_Precalc_Figure_01_02_222-1958.jpg"/>
</media>

<para id="fs-id1165134378637">window: <m:math>
<m:mrow>
<m:mo stretchy="false">[</m:mo><m:mn>0.1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.5em"/><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">]</m:mo><m:mo>;</m:mo></m:mrow>
</m:math> range: <m:math>
<m:mrow>
<m:mo stretchy="false">[</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.5em"/><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">]</m:mo></m:mrow>
</m:math>
</para>
</solution>
</exercise><exercise id="fs-id1165131911953">
<problem id="fs-id1165137842479">
<para id="fs-id1165137842481">Graph <m:math>
<m:mrow>
<m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac>
<m:mn>1</m:mn>
<m:mi>x</m:mi>
</m:mfrac>
</m:mrow>
</m:math> on the viewing window <m:math>
<m:mrow>
<m:mo stretchy="false">[</m:mo><m:mn>−0.5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>−0.1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">]</m:mo></m:mrow>
</m:math> and <m:math>
<m:mrow>
<m:mo stretchy="false">[</m:mo><m:mn>0.1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mspace width="0.5em"/><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">]</m:mo><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow>
</m:math> Determine the corresponding range for the viewing window. Show the graphs.</para></problem>
</exercise>
</section>
